;&lt;/path&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&#13;&#10; &lt;a href="https://kick.com/propovcs2" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="Kick" title="Kick"&gt;&lt;svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"&gt;&lt;path fill="currentColor" d="M1.333 0h8v5.333H12V2.667h2.667V0h8v8H20v2.667h-2.667v2.666H20V16h2.667v8h-8v-2.667H12v-2.666H9.333V24h-8Z"&gt;&lt;/path&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&#13;&#10;&lt;/div&gt;</description></item><item><title>CV</title><link>https://jparedesds.com/cv/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><author>jparedescolmenarejo@gmail.com (Jose Paredes)</author><guid>https://jparedesds.com/cv/</guid><description>&lt;header class="cvHead"&gt;&#10; &lt;h1&gt;CV&lt;/h1&gt;&#10; &lt;a class="cvDownload" href="https://jparedesds.com/resume.pdf" download aria-label="Download the PDF CV"&gt;&lt;svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"&gt;&lt;path fill="currentColor" d="M5 20h14v-2H5v2zm7-18v12.17l4.59-4.58L18 10l-7 7-7-7 1.41-1.41L11 14.17V2z"&gt;&lt;/path&gt;&lt;/svg&gt; PDF&lt;/a&gt;&#10;&lt;/header&gt;&#10;&lt;h3 id="contact-information"&gt;Contact Information&lt;/h3&gt;&#10;&lt;table class="cvFacts"&gt;&#10; &lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;Name&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;Jose Paredes Colmenarejo&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&#10; &lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;Professional title&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;Computer Vision &amp;amp; ML Engineer&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&#10; &lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;Email&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;jparedescolmenarejo@gmail.com&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&#10; &lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;Location&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;Madrid, Spain&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&#10; &lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;Links&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;GitHub · LinkedIn · Hugging Face · Kaggle&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&#10;&lt;/table&gt;&#10;&lt;h3 id="professional-summary"&gt;Professional Summary&lt;/h3&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Computer vision and ML engineer based in Madrid, working on industrial quality control and local-first AI products. I build YOLO-based inspection models, the data pipelines around them and the internal tools that put them to work. Open-source contributor with 33+ public repositories and 10+ computer-vision models published on Hugging Face.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Privacy</title><link>https://jparedesds.com/privacy/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><author>jparedescolmenarejo@gmail.com (Jose Paredes)</author><guid>https://jparedesds.com/privacy/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;This site is a personal portfolio run by &lt;strong&gt;Jose Paredes&lt;/strong&gt;, based in Madrid, Spain. It has no accounts, no comments and no newsletter, and no data is sold. This page explains what is collected when you visit, why, and how to opt out.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;h2 id="google-analytics-only-with-your-consent"&gt;Google Analytics (only with your consent)&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;The site uses Google Analytics 4 (measurement ID &lt;code&gt;G-Y85VJ3E6W4&lt;/code&gt;) to understand how the site is used: which pages are read, how visitors arrive and which content is useful. The legal basis is your consent: the analytics script loads &lt;strong&gt;only after you accept&lt;/strong&gt; the cookie banner. If you decline, it never loads.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Projects</title><link>https://jparedesds.com/projects/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><author>jparedescolmenarejo@gmail.com (Jose Paredes)</author><guid>https://jparedesds.com/projects/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;Three builds, each with the problem, what I did and the result. Everything here is live or in production.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;h2 id="case-studies"&gt;Case studies&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="caseList"&gt;&#10;&lt;section class="case"&gt;&#10;&lt;h3 id="vision"&gt;Industrial computer vision&lt;/h3&gt;&#10;&lt;figure class="caseMedia"&gt;&#10; &lt;img src="https://jparedesds.com/images/case-vision.svg" alt="Diagram of an industrial vision pipeline: camera frames become a labelled dataset, YOLO11 detects defects, and inspection decides pass or fail." width="1200" height="675"&gt;&#10; &lt;figcaption&gt;camera → dataset → YOLO11 → inspection&lt;/figcaption&gt;&#10;&lt;/figure&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Problem.&lt;/strong&gt; Penetrant and weld inspection depends on a trained eye: defects are small, varied and easy to miss at production pace.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What I did.&lt;/strong&gt; Trained YOLO11 detectors for fluorescent penetrant indications and welding defects, and published 10+ models on Hugging Face.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Result.&lt;/strong&gt; In production — the detectors run on real inspection work, not a benchmark.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;ul class="caseChips"&gt;&#10; &lt;li&gt;YOLO11&lt;/li&gt;&#10; &lt;li&gt;Hugging Face&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;/ul&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://huggingface.co/jparedesDS/fluorescent-penetrant-inspection" target="_blank" rel="noopener"&gt;Penetrant model on Hugging Face&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href="https://huggingface.co/jparedesDS" target="_blank" rel="noopener"&gt;More models&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href="https://github.com/jparedesDS/welding-defects-detection" target="_blank" rel="noopener"&gt;Welding detector on GitHub&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;/section&gt;&#10;&lt;section class="case"&gt;&#10;&lt;h3 id="docflow"&gt;DocFlow — document control SaaS&lt;/h3&gt;&#10;&lt;figure class="caseMedia"&gt;&#10; &lt;img src="https://jparedesds.com/images/case-docflow.svg" alt="DocFlow architecture diagram: email and the ERP exchange data with a FastAPI backend of 21 routers and 24 services, a React frontend of 24 screens, and DocuSign for signatures; deployed with Docker and CI." width="1200" height="675" loading="lazy"&gt;&#10; &lt;figcaption&gt;email / ERP ↔ FastAPI ↔ React · DocuSign · Docker + CI&lt;/figcaption&gt;&#10;&lt;/figure&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Problem.&lt;/strong&gt; Engineering project orders generate documents that must be tracked, reviewed and signed across email and the ERP.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What I did.&lt;/strong&gt; Built the internal SaaS end to end: a FastAPI backend with 21 API routers and 24 services, a React frontend with 24 screens, DocuSign for signatures, JWT auth, and Docker + CI for deployment.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Result.&lt;/strong&gt; In production and in daily use.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;ul class="caseChips"&gt;&#10; &lt;li&gt;FastAPI&lt;/li&gt;&#10; &lt;li&gt;React&lt;/li&gt;&#10; &lt;li&gt;DocuSign&lt;/li&gt;&#10; &lt;li&gt;JWT&lt;/li&gt;&#10; &lt;li&gt;Docker&lt;/li&gt;&#10; &lt;li&gt;CI&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;/ul&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;The public repository is DocFlow Lite, a CustomTkinter desktop app; the SaaS described here is internal.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://github.com/jparedesDS/docflow" target="_blank" rel="noopener"&gt;DocFlow Lite on GitHub&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;/section&gt;&#10;&lt;section class="case"&gt;&#10;&lt;h3 id="subany"&gt;subany.video — subtitles in the browser&lt;/h3&gt;&#10;&lt;figure class="caseMedia"&gt;&#10; &lt;img src="https://jparedesds.com/images/case-subany.png" alt="Screenshot of the subany.video home page: a field to paste a stream link and watch it with subtitles, processed locally in the browser." width="1200" height="675" loading="lazy"&gt;&#10; &lt;figcaption&gt;subany.video — paste a link, watch it subtitled.&lt;/figcaption&gt;&#10;&lt;/figure&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Problem.&lt;/strong&gt; Live streams have no subtitles in the viewer&amp;rsquo;s language, and server-side transcription adds cost and latency.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What I did.&lt;/strong&gt; Built a fixed-delay player with Whisper speech recognition, Silero VAD and ONNX/WebGPU inference — all in the browser, no servers.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Result.&lt;/strong&gt; Measured 15.3 s fixed delay against a 15 s target, with a median subtitle offset of 0–40 ms.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;ul class="caseChips"&gt;&#10; &lt;li&gt;Whisper&lt;/li&gt;&#10; &lt;li&gt;Silero VAD&lt;/li&gt;&#10; &lt;li&gt;ONNX/WebGPU&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;/ul&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://subany.video/" target="_blank" rel="noopener"&gt;Open subany.video&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href="https://jparedesds.com/blog/2026/11/09/how-subany-video-works/"&gt;How it works&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;/section&gt;&#10;&lt;/div&gt;</description></item><item><title>Repositories</title><link>https://jparedesds.com/repositories/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><author>jparedescolmenarejo@gmail.com (Jose Paredes)</author><guid>https://jparedesds.com/repositories/</guid><description/></item></channel></rss>